Architecture plan for Issues #224-#227: Blog article layout and typography refinements

Scope and module structure
- Shared page chrome:
  - `rust-backend/templates/partials/header.html` owns the top navigation logo.
  - `rust-backend/templates/partials/footer.html` owns the footer logo and newsletter area.
  - Issue #224 should update only logo display sizing classes/attributes in these partials; keep the existing Ideavibes hosted logo URL and alt text.
- Public article page:
  - `rust-backend/templates/public/post.html` owns the article title, rendered markdown insertion point, cover image, and attribution cards.
  - Issue #225 should reduce only the page-level post title class, avoiding changes to homepage/post-card headings.
  - Issue #227 should change the attribution `<aside>` layout from responsive two-column to a single-column stack so the author and company cards each span the full article width.
- Markdown rendering:
  - `rust-backend/src/html/markdown.rs` converts markdown to sanitized HTML and wraps it in `.article-prose`.
  - `assets/styles/input.css` defines Tailwind component styles; generated CSS is committed in `public/assets/app.css` after `npm run build:css`.
  - Issue #226 should style `.article-prose h1`, `.article-prose h2`, and `.article-prose h3` so rendered markdown headings are visually distinct after Tailwind base resets.
- Tests/build:
  - Use plain Rust backend tooling (`cargo test --manifest-path rust-backend/Cargo.toml`) and CSS generation (`npm run build:css`).
  - Existing markdown tests already verify `#` becomes `<h1>`; add/adjust tests only if implementation changes renderer behavior.

Dependencies between issues
- #224 is independent and can be implemented first because it touches shared partials only.
- #225 and #227 both edit `rust-backend/templates/public/post.html`; apply sequentially to avoid small template conflicts.
- #226 depends conceptually on the existing `.article-prose` wrapper from `markdown.rs`, but does not require renderer changes unless malformed markdown support is explicitly requested.
- CSS changes for #226 require regenerating `public/assets/app.css`; template-only issues do not require CSS rebuild unless new Tailwind classes are introduced that are not already emitted.

Key design decisions
- Product brand remains Ideavibes as used in the existing templates and issue text.
- Prefer minimal template class changes over adding new components for one-off sizing/layout tweaks.
- Keep markdown sanitization in Rust unchanged for security; solve heading presentation in CSS, not by injecting classes into user-authored markdown HTML.
- Use repo-native Tailwind component styles for article prose headings so future markdown content automatically renders `#`, `##`, and `###` consistently.
- Make the author/company cards full-width by removing the medium-screen two-column grid rather than duplicating card markup or changing backend context types.
